<Doc
  title="Privacy Policy · scrnsvr"
  description="How ScrnSvr handles your information."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Effective October 6, 2026</p>

  <p>ScrnSvr is made by Sanctum Labs, Inc. ("we", "us"). This policy explains what information the ScrnSvr iOS app and the scrnsvr.art website collect, how we use it, and the choices you have. If you have any questions, email <a href="mailto:support@scrnsvr.art">support@scrnsvr.art</a>.</p>

  <p><strong>The short version:</strong> we collect only what's needed to run your account. Which apps you shield and how you use them stay on your iPhone and are never sent to us. We don't sell your information, show ads, or track you across other apps and websites.</p>

  <h2>Information you give us</h2>
  <h3>Your account</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sign in with Apple:</strong> Apple shares an email address with us, which may be a private relay address if you chose to hide your email, and your name if you chose to share it.</li>
    <li><strong>Email sign-up:</strong> your email address and a password. Passwords are stored by our authentication provider in hashed form; we never see them.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Your profile</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The @handle you choose. Handles are unique, so the app can tell you when one is already taken.</li>
    <li>The profile picture you upload, if you add one. The app only accesses the photo you pick.</li>
    <li>The "object of your attention" text you post, if you post one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information that stays on your device</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Screen Time.</strong> ScrnSvr uses Apple's Screen Time framework to shield the apps you choose. Apple gives ScrnSvr opaque tokens in place of app names, and your selection, shield settings and usage information never leave your iPhone.</li>
    <li><strong>Shield activity.</strong> The number of times you open a shield, the breaks you take and the minutes you choose are counted on your iPhone to show your stats in the app. They are not sent to us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>When the app loads artworks, or you visit scrnsvr.art, our hosting providers receive standard technical information such as your IP address, device type and the time of the request, as part of delivering the content and keeping the service secure.</p>
  <p>If the app crashes or runs into an error, it sends a crash report so we can fix it. A report describes what went wrong, along with your device model, iOS version and app version. It doesn't include your name, email address, account or the apps you use, and we don't use it to identify you. We don't use analytics or advertising trackers.</p>

  <h2>On our website</h2>
  <p>If you join the waitlist on scrnsvr.art, we store the email address and phone number you enter so we can tell you when ScrnSvr is available. To be removed from the waitlist, email <a href="mailto:support@scrnsvr.art">support@scrnsvr.art</a>.</p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To create and secure your account and let you sign in.</li>
    <li>To show your profile in the app.</li>
    <li>To respond when you contact us.</li>
    <li>To keep ScrnSvr working, fix problems and protect against abuse.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't sell or rent your information, and we don't use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share information only with the service providers that run ScrnSvr on our behalf, and only as needed for them to do so:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong>: account sign-in, our database and file storage, including profile pictures and the artworks.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple</strong>: Sign in with Apple, and the Screen Time framework, which runs on your device.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting for scrnsvr.art.</li>
    <li><strong>Sentry</strong>: crash and error reports from the app.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may also disclose information if required by law, or to protect the rights and safety of our users or others.</p>

  <h2>Keeping and deleting your information</h2>
  <p>We keep your account information for as long as you have an account. You can delete your account at any time in the app: open <strong>Profile</strong>, tap the settings icon, then <strong>Delete account</strong>. This permanently deletes your account, your @handle and your profile picture, and, for Sign in with Apple accounts, revokes ScrnSvr's access to your Apple ID. Copies may remain in our providers' backups for a limited time before they are overwritten.</p>
  <p>Information stored only on your device, such as your Screen Time selection and shield stats, is removed when you delete the app.</p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You can view and change your profile in the app at any time, and delete your account as described above. Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to request a copy of your information, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to how we use it. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:support@scrnsvr.art">support@scrnsvr.art</a>. We'll respond within the time the law requires.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>We use industry-standard measures, including encryption in transit, to protect your information. No method of storage or transmission is completely secure, but we work to protect your information and limit who can access it.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>ScrnSvr's art is suitable for all ages. Accounts, which include an email address and can include a profile picture, are for people 13 and older, or the minimum age in your country if it's higher. We don't knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has created an account, contact us and we'll delete it.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we'll update the effective date above. If a change materially affects how we handle your information, we'll let you know in the app before it takes effect.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Sanctum Labs, Inc.<br /><a href="mailto:support@scrnsvr.art">support@scrnsvr.art</a></p>
</Doc>
